# `script-shell=E:\Freebuff\node-v20.18.1-win-x64\node.exe` used to be set here.
# node.exe is not a shell: npm ran every package script as `node "<script text>"`
# and each one failed with MODULE_NOT_FOUND (`npm run typecheck`, `build`, `test`,
# `lint`, `test:e2e` were all unusable). npm now uses its default Windows shell.
#
# Note: package scripts invoke local binaries through node_modules/.bin, so the
# Node.js directory must be on PATH when running npm scripts.
